Title: THE THRESHOLD
Author: Morgan Blake
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. FARMHOUSE - ESTABLISHING - DUSK

Remote county road. One light in an upper window — no power on record.

EXT. FARMHOUSE PORCH - DUSK

ELISE VOSS sets EMF gear. DAN films B-roll, unconvinced.
ELISE
Three families. Same bedroom. Same exit story.

INT. LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Interviews on camera — former tenant: The door wouldn't stay open.

INT. UPSTAIRS HALL - NIGHT

Breath fog. The THRESHOLD of the east bedroom pulses dark.
DAN
Cracked window. Draft.

INT. EAST BEDROOM - NIGHT

Elise crosses the line. Recorder captures a child's warning.
ON RECORDER — CHILD
Don't let her close the door.

INT. UPSTAIRS HALL - NIGHT

Dan turns — hall longer than before. Elise behind him, though she never left the room on his feed.

INT. EAST BEDROOM - NIGHT

Floorboard pried. Child's DRAWING — THE OTHER SIDE OF AWAKE.
ELISE
A door. Left open.

INT. LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Gear spins wild. Dan's camera catches a woman in period dress — not in the room when they blink.
DAN
We leave. We leave now.

EXT. PORCH - NIGHT

They stumble out. Upstairs window slams shut — from inside.

INT. EAST BEDROOM - NIGHT

Camera left behind keeps recording. The THRESHOLD flares. A small hand reaches through, closes the door gently — latched from the other side.
ON RECORDER — CHILD
Thank you for not closing it.

FADE OUT.


THE END
